––– comment –––
Issue #5066: sequential HTTP bulk REPLACE operations with IDs on both sides of
2^63 must never leave duplicate or stale documents while RAM chunks are being
saved in the background. Use a small rt_mem_limit and disable auto-merges to
exercise postponed kills during SaveDiskChunk. Repeated independent trials
reduce the chance of missing the background-save overlap on slower machines.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
